{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792429652,"nonce":"yOHAlWGp3dYbVMYJa2diEnVHFXo=","message":"Inspected the user's ASH_GC_DEBUG_ROOTS report at gc.log. The final full collection (#27, 68.87s) reports 504.0 MB live and frees only 43 blocks. Root paths for large CanvasPainter and Mesh buffers reach ashui.reactive.Watch's static bySlot array. For example, gc.log:28556-28590 traces an 18454 KB float buffer through Mesh -\u003e CanvasPainter -\u003e Canvas -\u003e CodeEditor -\u003e Interaction -\u003e Owner -\u003e Watch -\u003e ArrayObj -\u003e ashui.reactive.$Watch. gc.log:28590-28620 shows the shorter Canvas -\u003e Watch -\u003e static-array path. This is reachable UI data; the report does not establish a collector tracing failure.\n\nCanvas and CanvasPainter each occur 74 times across the report, but those occurrences identify four distinct objects, not 74 leaked canvases. The log alone does not identify whether the relevant tab was closed or its owner disposed, and includes other root paths (for example the renderer/glyph atlas through ThemeState). Do not equate sampled root-chain counts with an exhaustive accounting of the whole live set.\n\nSource inspection of pinned Ashui f2671d0: Watch.stop already nulls bySlot[slot] and releases the native effect. Owner.dispose invokes registered cleanups. Thus the static array does not unconditionally retain every watch ever created; a surviving watch needs its ownership/cleanup path investigated. Constructor cleanup registration occurs only after the initial read and reaction, so an exception before that point is a separate lifecycle hole worth testing upstream; it has not been reproduced as the cause of this log.\n\nExpanded tests/InteractionProbe.hx to count non-null Watch registry entries, registered CodeEditors and disposed component hosts, and to close history plus all ten code tabs and repeat code-tab open/close cycles. Pinned Ashui, installed Ash, dark scheme: history-ready = 7793 watches / 10 editors / 13 canvases; history closed = 7660 / 10 / 12; all editors closed and Explorer restored = 456 / 0 / 0. Three subsequent reopen/close cycles each go 1204 / 1 / 2 -\u003e 456 / 0 / 0. No disposed component hosts remain registered. This fixture does not reproduce watches surviving closed tabs. Evidence: bin/interaction-watch-retention/results.json. These counts do not prove all framework references have been released and are not an AOT reproduction of the user's workload.\n\nThe pinned CodeMinimap creates its Canvas with retain=true, disabling CanvasPainter's idle release of CPU mesh/upload buffers for still-open tabs. CanvasPainter.dispose does release that storage on actual disposal. The sibling Ashui checkout already has an uncommitted CodeMinimap change removing retain=true; no sibling source was edited here, and no dependency pin was changed. Request upstream coverage for idle minimap CPU-buffer release, normal owner disposal, and watches whose initial callbacks throw. Keep this memory issue open pending the upstream change and the real workload recheck; GC tuning is not a demonstrated fix for the reachable buffers in this report.","files":null}]}